Blobferry changes to the Arm vulkan-wsi-layer (gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/vulkan-wsi-layer, MIT).
Base: upstream commit f5148d4 ("Merge 'Fix present-stage timestamp calibration' into 'main'"), pinned as the
third_party/vulkan-wsi-layer submodule. build-wsi.sh applies this patch when it is not applied yet.

- Works with gamescope's Wayland and the vendor Mali driver: explicit sync is optional (used when the compositor
  offers zwp_linux_explicit_synchronization_v1), missing WSI device extensions are a warning instead of an error,
  xlib/xcb are left to other layers (only win32 stays unsupported here).
- dma_buf_heaps allocator: falls back to a read-only open of /dev/dma_heap/<heap> when read-write is denied.
- CMake: WAYLAND_PROTOCOLS_DIR can be given instead of found through pkg-config (cross builds).
- Acquire with timeout UINT64_MAX waits again instead of returning VK_TIMEOUT/VK_NOT_READY (vkd3d-proton asserts
  on those); a sticky error from the page-flip thread is no longer reported to the app as success; a present whose
  GPU work takes over 2 s is logged (after 2, 10, 60 s, then every 5 min) instead of hanging silently.
- MALI_WSI_NO_10BIT=1 hides the 10-bit surface formats.
- MALI_WSI_PROBE_PIXELS=1 (debug) logs pixel samples of the first presented images.

